From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:08:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Build the EROFS tools with Zstandard

The upstream sources support Zstandard (lib/compressor_libzstd.c and the
decoder in lib/decompress.c), but the Android build leaves the encoder out
and does not define HAVE_LIBZSTD, so mkfs.erofs rejects -zzstd and
fsck.erofs cannot read a Zstandard image. Compile the encoder, define
the feature next to the other compressors, and link libzstd: statically
for the host tools, as a shared library on the device and in recovery.

AOSP's zstd.h marks ZSTD_getDecompressedSize deprecated, which the
module's -Werror turns into an error in lib/decompress.c. The library's
own switch silences the notice.
---
 Android.bp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 7ca293faae2fef1166c5a0e0383a576af3030a51..2f87a496fdcf20d4af52675c8c0903923434a6fe 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@ cc_defaults {
         "-DHAVE_LINUX_TYPES_H",
         "-DHAVE_LIBSELINUX",
         "-DHAVE_LIBUUID",
+        "-DHAVE_LIBZSTD",
+        "-DZSTD_DISABLE_DEPRECATE_WARNINGS",
         "-DLZ4_ENABLED",
         "-DLZ4HC_ENABLED",
         "-DWITH_ANDROID",
@@ -105,6 +107,7 @@ cc_defaults {
                 "liblog",
                 "liblz4",
                 "libselinux",
+                "libzstd",
             ],
             stl: "none",
         },
@@ -116,6 +119,7 @@ cc_defaults {
                 "liblog",
                 "liblz4",
                 "libselinux",
+                "libzstd",
             ],
             stl: "c++_static",
         },
@@ -132,7 +136,6 @@ cc_library {
     ],
     exclude_srcs: [
         "lib/compressor_libdeflate.c",
-        "lib/compressor_libzstd.c",
     ],
     export_include_dirs: ["include"],
 
